    "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nEach data-parallel replica now gets a separate HTTP port when the embedded Rust server is enabled. Previously the listener used `attn_dp_rank`, which is zero on every replica when attention data parallelism is off, so `--dp-size 2` made both servers try port 30000 and left port 30001 unavailable.\r\n\r\nThe fix uses `dp_rank`, which already holds the replica number. With attention data parallelism, the controller stores the computed attention rank in that same field, so the ports added by #33105 do not change; the existing `dp_size > 1` check also keeps single-replica and externally assigned ports unchanged.\r\n\r\n## Reproduction\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nSGLANG_RUST_SERVER=1 sglang serve \\\r\n  --model-path meta-llama/Llama-3.2-1B-Instruct \\\r\n  --dp-size 2\r\n\r\ncurl --fail http://127.0.0.1:30000/health\r\ncurl --fail http://127.0.0.1:30001/health\r\n```\r\n\r\nBefore the fix, the second scheduler reports that port 30000 is already in use and nothing listens on port 30001. After the fix, both health requests succeed.\r\n\r\ncc @rainj-me @sherlockwu \r\n\r\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #33204565534](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/33204565534)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #33204565187](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/33204565187)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 7.2): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd-rocm720:start -->:x: [Run #33204565261](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/33204565261)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd-rocm720:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
